<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Zhezong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1077">1077</a>–<a href="/years/1100">1100</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Zhezong of Song, Zhao Xu, Zhao Yong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Zhezong of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> (personal name Zhao Xu) was the seventh emperor of the Song dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, reigning from 1085 until his death in 1100. A son of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-shenzong-of-song">Shenzong</a>, he came to the throne as a child under his grandmother, Grand Empress Dowager Gao, whose conservative ministers reversed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-anshi">Wang Anshi</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-policies-song">New Policies</a>. After her death in 1093 he restored the reforms, named Zhang Dun grand chancellor and in 1094 renamed the era Shaosheng; the conservatives were purged and exiled, and the factional fighting intensified. His renewed war against the Western Xia expanded the Song to its greatest extent. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a> at 23 and was succeeded by his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-huizong">Huizong</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Child emperors were ruled by empress dowagers, as <b>Zhezong</b> was by his grandmother, the Grand Empress Dowager Gao, from 1085.</blockquote><a href="/societies/song-china">Social Hierarchy of Song China</a></li></ul></section>
